@title Wastewater Treatment Plant Upgrade: Steering Committee Status
@subtitle Week ending 2026-10-16
@date 2026-10-16
@width wide

## Overall status

! At risk

The project is not on track. Five of the seven unfinished work packages are forecast to finish late, and the last one, commissioning and training (WP-08), is forecast 35 days late, on 2027-09-17 instead of 2027-08-13. Total spending is in line with progress: 43.7% of the work-package budgets is spent and about 44% of the work is complete. That total hides two packages that have spent more than their work is worth: inlet works (WP-02) and the control system (WP-06). The tracker export has no forecast final cost, so this report compares spending with progress; it does not forecast the final bill.

kpi Work complete | 44% | budget-weighted | bar
kpi Budget spent | $7,259,210 | 42.7% of $16,985,500 | neutral
kpi Final finish | 2027-09-17 | +35 days | bad
kpi Contingency used | 28.4% | $787,300 left | neutral

## Decision needed from the committee

!! Approve $410,000 for early purchase of the blowers (WP-04) before the 6% price increase on Nov 1.

- A 6% increase on $410,000 is $24,600, if the increase applies to the whole order.
- Blower lead time is already 31 weeks, and WP-04 is forecast 14 days late.
- The tracker does not say where the $410,000 would come from. If it came from contingency, usage would rise from 28.4% to 65.7% ($722,700 of $1,100,000). Staff should confirm the funding source before the vote.

