WP-05 and WP-07 are forecast on their planned dates, but WP-07 has no owner and has not started, so its date is not yet backed by anyone.

## Cost: where the money is going

data prog = Package,Work complete,Budget spent; WP-01,100,103.5; WP-02,88,94.1; WP-03,61,58.5; WP-04,34,30.3; WP-05,12,9.4; WP-06,20,33.8; WP-07,0,0; WP-08,0,0

chart bar prog y=Work complete,Budget spent unit=% title="Work complete vs share of budget spent"

Two packages are spending faster than they progress. WP-06 (control system) has spent 33.8% of its budget at 20% complete. WP-02 (inlet works) has spent 94.1% at 88%. WP-01 is finished and closed 3.5% over budget ($191,420 against $185,000).

data value = Package,Spent,Value of work done (budget x % complete),Spent minus value; WP-01,"$191,420","$185,000","+$6,420"; WP-02,"$2,201,610","$2,059,200","+$142,410"; WP-03,"$2,288,330","$2,385,405","-$97,075"; WP-04,"$1,742,900","$1,958,400","-$215,500"; WP-05,"$133,250","$170,400","-$37,150"; WP-06,"$389,000","$230,000","+$159,000"; Total WP-01 to WP-06,"$6,946,510","$6,988,405","-$41,895"

table value title="Spent against the value of the work done (plus means spent more than the work is worth)"

The small net under-spend of $41,895 comes from WP-03, WP-04 and WP-05 spending less than their progress. That may be real savings or invoices that have not arrived yet; the tracker cannot tell us which. It should not be read as offsetting the $301,410 of over-spend on WP-02 and WP-06 and the $6,420 on WP-01.

## Contingency

kpi Contingency budget | $1,100,000
kpi Used to date | $312,700 | 28.4% | neutral
kpi Remaining | $787,300 | 71.6% | neutral

28.4% used and about 56% of the work still to do (the tracker note says about 55%) sounds comfortable, but the open risks are all in the remaining work: the blower price and 31-week lead time, the SCADA vendor change and integration risk, an unassigned odor control package, and the two packages already spending ahead of progress. The tracker does not show what the $312,700 has been used for, and the $410,000 blower decision above may draw on it.

## Safety, community and permits

- Two safety incidents this month, both minor: a cut finger, and a "near miss" with a crane lift on Oct 3.
- Neighbor complaint on Oct 8 about night noise from the pile driver, resolved with a 7 pm cutoff.
- The state permit inspector visits on Oct 29.

